<lesson id="les-l8-02-rain-fade" title="Rain on the long hop" level="8" minutes="12" goal="ProsperVillage stays under 20 milliseconds in heavy rain and survives losing the valley pair"/>
<step n="1" text="The wet season arrives, and rain fades the long valley hop between RegencyRadio and ProsperRadio. Model the fade: open the port settings of RegencyRadio FastEthernet1 and of ProsperRadio FastEthernet0, and raise the delay of each to 30000 microseconds."/>
<step n="2" text="Ping RegencyServices from ProsperResident and read the time: the faded hop pushes it past 30 milliseconds."/>
<step n="3" text="A relay tower on the hill splits the distance into two short hops that hold in the rain. Cable HillRadio FastEthernet0 to RegencyHub GigabitEthernet0/2, and HillRadio FastEthernet1 to PopProsperVillage GigabitEthernet0/2." check="c1"/>
<step n="4" text="Even if the faded valley pair drops out entirely, the hill relay must keep the village on." check="c2"/>
<check id="c1" kind="latency" from="pc0" to="server0" url="" expect="20" label="ProsperVillage answers in under 20 milliseconds, rain or not"/>
<check id="c2" kind="outage" from="pc0" to="server0" url="rh0:GigabitEthernet0/1" expect="ok" label="ProsperVillage still reaches RegencyServices with the valley pair cut"/>
